{
  "scenes": [
    {
      "role": "hook",
      "narration": "This animal has three hearts. Seriously.",
      "headline": "Three hearts?!",
      "highlight": [
        "Three"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "surprised",
        "pose": "jumping"
      },
      "from": 0,
      "durationInFrames": 107
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Meet the octopus! Eight arms, no bones, and inside its soft body, it has not one, but three hearts.",
      "headline": "The octopus",
      "highlight": [
        "octopus"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "excited",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "spotlight",
        "icon": "octopus",
        "caption": "Soft body, eight arms, three hearts"
      },
      "from": 107,
      "durationInFrames": 220
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Two small hearts push blood through the gills, where it picks up oxygen from the water.",
      "headline": "Two hearts for the gills",
      "highlight": [
        "Two hearts"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "iconGrid",
        "icon": "heart",
        "count": 3,
        "label": "hearts in one octopus"
      },
      "from": 327,
      "durationInFrames": 164
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Then the third heart, the big one, pumps that blood to the rest of its body.",
      "headline": "One heart for the body",
      "highlight": [
        "body"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "thinking",
        "pose": "idle"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "steps",
        "steps": [
          {
            "icon": "heart",
            "text": "Gill hearts pump"
          },
          {
            "icon": "wave",
            "text": "Blood grabs oxygen"
          },
          {
            "icon": "heart",
            "text": "Main heart pumps"
          },
          {
            "icon": "octopus",
            "text": "Whole body fed"
          }
        ]
      },
      "from": 491,
      "durationInFrames": 152
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Fun twist. When an octopus swims, that main heart stops beating. That may be why they prefer crawling!",
      "headline": "Swimming stops a heart",
      "highlight": [
        "stops"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "surprised",
        "pose": "idle"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "orbit",
        "center": "octopus",
        "satellite": "heart",
        "label": "Swimming is tiring for octopuses"
      },
      "from": 643,
      "durationInFrames": 218
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "And their blood is blue! It uses copper to carry oxygen. Our blood uses iron, so ours is red.",
      "headline": "Blue blood",
      "highlight": [
        "Blue"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "excited",
        "pose": "jumping"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "spotlight",
        "icon": "drop",
        "caption": "Copper in its blood makes it blue"
      },
      "from": 861,
      "durationInFrames": 215
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "One more thing. About two thirds of an octopus's brain cells are in its arms, not its head.",
      "headline": "Smart arms",
      "highlight": [
        "arms"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "wink",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "bigNumber",
        "value": 2,
        "unit": "out of 3",
        "label": "brain cells are in its arms",
        "icon": "brain"
      },
      "from": 1076,
      "durationInFrames": 195
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "So each arm can explore, touch, and taste things on its own. Like eight curious helpers!",
      "headline": "Eight curious arms",
      "highlight": [
        "Eight"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "waving"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "iconGrid",
        "icon": "hand",
        "count": 8,
        "label": "arms that explore on their own"
      },
      "from": 1271,
      "durationInFrames": 189
    },
    {
      "role": "recap",
      "narration": "Quick recap. Octopuses have three hearts, blue blood, and arms that can almost think for themselves.",
      "headline": "Quick recap",
      "highlight": [
        "recap"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "bullets": [
        "Three hearts",
        "Blue, copper-based blood",
        "Brainy arms"
      ],
      "from": 1460,
      "durationInFrames": 211
    },
    {
      "role": "cta",
      "narration": "Follow Pip for a new mind-blowing fact every day!",
      "headline": "A new fact every day!",
      "highlight": [
        "every day"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "waving"
      },
      "from": 1671,
      "durationInFrames": 189
    }
  ],
